---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import BlogLead from '@/components/blog/BlogLead.astro'
import BlogBody from '@/components/blog/BlogBody.astro'
import BlogRelated from '@/components/blog/BlogRelated.astro'

const post = {
 title: 'Custom Embroidered T-Shirts: When They\'re the Right Choice',
 description:
 'Compare embroidered t-shirts with screen-printed tees. Review exact products, artwork, placement, decoration compatibility, care, availability, pricing, and current order terms.',
 category: 'Products',
 readTime: '7 min read',
 date: 'May 9, 2026',
 isoDate: '2026-05-09',
 image: '/images/og-default.jpg',
 slug: 'custom-embroidered-t-shirts-buyer-guide',
}

const faqs = [
 { q: 'Can you embroider on a t-shirt?', a: 'Many t-shirts may support embroidery. The fabric, artwork, placement, and backing decide whether a tee can be embroidered. We check the garment and design first.' },
 { q: 'Should I embroider or screen print my custom t-shirts?', a: 'Compare both methods for the same garment, artwork, placement, quantity, feel, care, deadline, and current price. We will flag what works and quote each suitable option.' },
 { q: 'What\'s the best t-shirt for embroidery?', a: 'There is no universal best t-shirt. Compare exact products such as the Carhartt K87, Bayside 5100, and Hanes Beefy-T by fabric, fit, care, availability, price, and decoration compatibility.' },
 { q: 'Will embroidered t-shirts pucker over time?', a: 'The fabric, stitch density, and backing set the puckering risk. Review a proof or sample when appropriate. Follow the garment and decoration care instructions.' },
 { q: 'How does embroidered t-shirt cost compare to screen printed?', a: 'Commercial terms vary by garment, artwork, placement, colors, stitch count, quantity, partner, and deadline. Compare current written quotes for the same order. Do not rely on a fixed quantity threshold.' },
 { q: 'Can you embroider a back design on a t-shirt?', a: 'Some products and designs may support back embroidery. Ask us to compare methods, comfort, stitch count, care, price, and timing for your garment and artwork.' },
 { q: 'Where can I get custom embroidered t-shirts in Las Vegas?', a: 'Bighorn Threads gets embroidery done for Vegas contractors and service businesses. Carhartt K87, Bayside 5100, and Hanes Beefy-T are options to compare. Your quote confirms sizes, availability, and timing.' },
]

const schema = {
 '@context': 'https://schema.org',
 '@graph': [
 { '@type': 'Article', headline: post.title, description: post.description, image: `https://bighornthreads.com${post.image}`, datePublished: post.isoDate, dateModified: '2026-08-21', author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Bighorn Threads', url: 'https://bighornthreads.com/' }, publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Bighorn Threads', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://bighornthreads.com/images/logos/bighorn-logo-color.png' } }, mainEntityOfPage: `https://bighornthreads.com/blog/${post.slug}/` },
 { '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement: [{ '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://bighornthreads.com/' }, { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://bighornthreads.com/blog/' }, { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: post.title, item: `https://bighornthreads.com/blog/${post.slug}/` }] },
 { '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })) },
 ],
}

const speakableSchema = {
 '@context': 'https://schema.org',
 '@type': 'WebPage',
 url: `https://bighornthreads.com/blog/${post.slug}/`,
 name: post.title,
 speakable: {
  '@type': 'SpeakableSpecification',
  cssSelector: ['h1','.speakable-answer'],
 },
}
---

<BaseLayout title={post.title} description={post.description} canonical={`https://bighornthreads.com/blog/${post.slug}/`} ogImage={post.image} type="article" publishedDate={post.isoDate}>
 <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
 <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(speakableSchema)} />
 <article class="bg-concrete">
 <header class="post-head">
 <div class="post-head-inner">
 <div>
 <nav class="mb-6 font-mono text-xs text-ash" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/" class="hover:text-gold-700">Home</a><span class="px-2">/</span><a href="/blog/" class="hover:text-gold-700">Blog</a></nav>
 <span class="mb-3 inline-block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold-600">{post.category}</span>
 <h1 class="mb-6 font-heading text-3xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl">{post.title}</h1>
 <p class="mb-8 text-xl leading-relaxed text-ash">When embroidered tees are worth the cost, when to screen print instead, and which blanks take embroidery cleanly.</p>
 <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 border-t border-hairline pt-6 font-mono text-sm text-ash"><span class="text-gold-600">Bighorn Threads Team</span><span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span>{post.readTime}</span><span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><time datetime={post.isoDate}>{post.date}</time></div>
 </div>
 <BlogLead />
 </div>
 </header>
 <BlogBody>

 <aside class="mb-10 border border-hairline bg-panel p-7">
 <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold-600">Quick Answer</p>
 <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal sm:text-xl speakable-answer">Embroider a tee when you want a small, textured chest logo on a heavier shirt. Screen print it when the design is big, covers the back, or the order is large. Thin, stretchy tees are the ones that pucker under thread.</p>
 </aside>

 <h2 id="when-to-embroider" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">When Embroidered Tees Make Sense</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Embroidery tends to fit when you want:</p>
 <ul class="mb-6 list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 <li><strong>A textured chest logo.</strong> Thread looks more finished up close than ink.</li>
 <li><strong>A smaller order.</strong> There are no screens to set up, though a new logo needs digitizing.</li>
 <li><strong>A service-tech look.</strong> A stitched logo and name read as a uniform at a customer’s door.</li>
 <li><strong>A logo on a rated tee.</strong> Only if the garment maker allows it, and thread alone doesn’t protect a rating.</li>
 <li><strong>Tees with chest-only designs.</strong> When there's no need for a back logo or large design.</li>
 </ul>

 <h2 id="when-to-print" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">When Screen Printing Wins on Tees</h2>
 <ul class="mb-6 list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 <li><strong>Full-back designs.</strong> Thread at that size gets stiff and costly, so compare <a href="/services/screen-printing-las-vegas/" class="text-gold-600 underline decoration-gold-600/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-gold-600">screen printing</a> instead.</li>
 <li><strong>Larger quantities.</strong> Screen setup spreads across the run, so the price per shirt falls as the count rises.</li>
 <li><strong>Large bold designs.</strong> Block letters, simple shapes, oversized graphics print well and look intentional.</li>
 <li><strong>Complex multi-color art.</strong> Ask us to price screen printing against DTF.</li>
 <li><strong>Field crew tees that get replaced often.</strong> A print on a heavy tee costs less to replace.</li>
 </ul>

 <h2 id="best-blanks" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">T-Shirt Blanks to Compare for Embroidery</h2>

 <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Carhartt K87 Workwear Pocket Tee</h3>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">A heavy cotton work tee with a chest pocket. Keep the logo clear of the pocket. See our <a href="/blog/carhartt-custom-embroidery-las-vegas/" class="text-gold-600 underline decoration-gold-600/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-gold-600">Carhartt custom embroidery</a> guide.</p>

 <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Bayside 5100 Heavyweight Tee</h3>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">A heavyweight tee that gives thread a stable base.</p>

 <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Hanes Beefy-T (5180)</h3>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">A familiar heavyweight cotton tee, and a good one to compare against the two above.</p>

 <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Performance / Moisture-Wicking Tees</h3>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Carhartt Force and Sport-Tek PosiCharge are two to compare. Thin performance fabric puckers more easily, so keep the logo simple and approve a sample.</p>

 <h2 id="placement" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Placement and Sizing</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Common placements:</p>
 <ul class="mb-6 list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 <li><strong>Left chest:</strong> The standard spot for a company logo.</li>
 <li><strong>Right chest:</strong> Employee name (for service tech roles)</li>
 <li><strong>Sleeve:</strong> Optional secondary mark</li>
 <li><strong>Back yoke:</strong> Possible but uncommon: embroidery scaled to a back logo gets expensive</li>
 </ul>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Avoid placements that put dense embroidery on stretchy fabric panels (sides, lower back), where pucker risk is higher.</p>

 <h2 id="costs" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">What Embroidered Tees Cost</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">The garment, artwork, placement, stitch count, quantity, and deadline set the price. See <a href="/blog/how-much-to-embroider-a-shirt/" class="text-gold-600 underline decoration-gold-600/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-gold-600">how much it costs to embroider a shirt</a> for factors to confirm.</p>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Send the shirt, your logo, and the count, and your quote will list each charge.</p>

 <div class="mt-12 border border-hairline bg-gold-500/5 p-7 sm:p-9">
 <h2 class="mb-3 font-heading text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Custom embroidered tees in Las Vegas</h2>
<p class="mb-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Bighorn Threads gets custom t-shirts embroidered with your logo. Send your logo and count for a price and a proof.</p>
 <a href="/get-a-quote/" class="inline-flex min-h-[48px] items-center gap-2 bg-gold-500 px-7 py-3 text-base font-bold text-charcoal transition-all hover:bg-gold-600">Get a Quote →</a>
 </div>
 </BlogBody>
 </article>
<BlogRelated />
</BaseLayout>
